From f4e07f88994105b266093e138533178962805e36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab bringup <bringup@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:09:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kebab: correct the rear camera comment
 block

The header still described the D-PHY four-lane plan and the pin numbers
from the first (wrong) DTBO reading: RESET tlmm145 and VANA tlmm26.  The
node itself has been C-PHY three-trio on tlmm78/139/117 for a while, so
the comment now matches the code and says plainly that the trio count
still needs frame capture on this board to be believed.

Comments only: the compiled DTB is byte-identical (c42f8555...).
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts    | 21 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
index 9ea6bea63..4b4a84fb2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
@@ -1773,17 +1773,20 @@ &cci1 {
  */
 /*
  * Rear main 48 MP camera: Sony IMX586 on CCI0 master 0 / CSIPHY0
- * (vendor fragment@88: csiphy-sd-index = <0>, cci-master = <0>, GPIO labels
- * CAM_MCLK0=tlmm94, CAM_RESET0=tlmm145, CAM_VANA=tlmm26).
+ * (vendor fragment@88: csiphy-sd-index = <0>, cci-master = <0>; control pins
+ * from this device's own DTBO, see the gpio block below:
+ * CAM_MCLK0=tlmm94, CAM_RESET0=tlmm78, CAM_CUSTOM1=tlmm139, CAM_VDIG=tlmm117).
  *
- * The link is described as D-PHY with four lanes because that is the only
- * signalling mode the 7.2 CAMSS drivers can currently program (the CSID
- * driver never sets its C-PHY PHY_TYPE_SEL bit). If the board turns out to
- * use C-PHY this node has to change together with a CSID/CSIPHY patch; the
- * driver itself accepts both.
+ * The link is described as C-PHY with three trios: the sensor driver picks
+ * the lane mode from the endpoint bus-type, and CAMSS was patched
+ * (patches/camera/0002) so an SM8250 CSIPHY programs a three-phase link
+ * instead of rejecting C-PHY.  The D-PHY alternative (four lanes plus
+ * clock-lanes = <7>) is what the v3c trial image uses and is not described
+ * here.
  *
- * Lane order <1 2 3 4> mirrors the working front IMX471 endpoint on this
- * board; the rear assignment still has to be confirmed by capturing frames.
+ * Lane order <0 1 2> and the three-trio count come from the hotdog community
+ * port of the same IMX586 module; they still have to be confirmed by
+ * capturing frames on this board.
  */
 &cci0_i2c0 {
 	/* Sony IMX parts on this board are specified for 400 kHz. */
-- 
